# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALLOWLIST. Nothing is tracked unless it is named below.
#
# The README says this repo "only tracks intentionally selected files". A
# denylist cannot deliver that: it tracks whatever nobody thought to exclude, so
# the first mistake is a leak. This file inverts the default instead.
#
#   *      ignore every file, everywhere
#   !*/    but still descend into directories, so a re-include below can be
#          reached (git will not look inside an ignored directory)
#   !path  re-include exactly one file
#
# Consequences worth knowing before editing:
#
#   - Adding a file to the repo is TWO steps. `git add newfile` will refuse
#     ("ignored by one of your .gitignore files") until you add a `!` line for
#     it here. That refusal is the feature: every tracked file is a decision.
#   - `git status` stays quiet about junk - build output, downloaded archives,
#     an app that dumped a cache into a config directory - instead of inviting
#     you to `git add -A` it by accident.
#   - Paths starting with `/` are anchored to the repo root, so `!/zshrc`
#     cannot accidentally re-include some other directory's `zshrc`.
#   - Bulk directory re-includes are avoided on purpose. `!/config/**` would
#     hand back the whole subtree, which is denylist behaviour again.
#
# The defensive patterns at the bottom are redundant while the allowlist holds -
# they exist for when it does not. If a future edit re-includes a directory in
# bulk, those patterns are the second line of defence that still keeps
# credentials, keys, histories and databases out.
#
# Run `bin/dotfiles-doctor --only scan` before pushing; CI additionally fails if
# any tracked file matches an ignore rule (an allowlist hole) and runs gitleaks
# over the full history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*
!*/


# ---- repo documentation and bootstrap inputs ----
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/setup.md
!/manifest.tsv
!/Brewfile
!/Brewfile.optional
!/install.sh

# ---- CI ----
!/.github/workflows/ci.yml

# ---- scripts (installed to ~/bin, must stay mode 755) ----
!/bin/dotfiles-doctor
!/bin/rebuild-alttab

# ---- shell ----
!/zshenv
!/zshrc
!/zprofile
!/profile

# ---- vim ----
!/vimrc
!/vim/plugins.txt
!/vim/templates/skeleton.c
!/vim/templates/skeleton.cpp
!/vim/templates/skeleton.rkt
!/vim/templates/skeleton.rmd
!/vim/templates/skeleton.tex

# ---- git ----
!/gitconfig
!/config/git/ignore

# ---- agents ----
!/agents/AGENTS.md
!/agents/claude/settings.json
!/agents/codex/config.toml
!/agents/reference/*
!/agents/skills/autopush/SKILL.md
!/agents/skills/find-skills/SKILL.md
!/agents/skills/gh-stack/SKILL.md
!/agents/skills/memdump/SKILL.md
!/agents/skills/memload/SKILL.md
!/agents/skills/pr_update/SKILL.md

# ---- per-tool config ----
!/config/starship.toml
!/config/ghostty/config.ghostty
!/config/docker/daemon.json
!/config/fish/conf.d/uv.env.fish
!/config/gh/config.yml
!/config/gnupg/common.conf
!/config/ssh/config
!/config/vscode/settings.json
!/config/yt-dlp/config

# ---- neovim, staged but not active ----
!/config/nvim-staged/init.lua
!/config/nvim-staged/init.vim.bak
!/config/nvim-staged/lazy-lock.json
!/config/nvim-staged/lua/plugins/editing.lua
!/config/nvim-staged/lua/plugins/git.lua
!/config/nvim-staged/lua/plugins/langs.lua
!/config/nvim-staged/lua/plugins/lsp.lua
!/config/nvim-staged/lua/plugins/treesitter.lua
!/config/nvim-staged/lua/plugins/ui.lua


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Denylist, second line of defence. These come AFTER the allowlist so the last
# matching pattern wins and they override any `!` re-include above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generated machine state, not configuration: install timestamps, the
# last-selected agent list, dismissed prompts. It changes on its own and it
# describes one machine, so it does not belong in a portable repo.
# Untracked as of this commit (`git rm --cached agents/skill-lock.json`); the
# working file is left in place because the skills CLI owns it. Note it is still
# reachable in history at 607fc40 - this pattern stops future leaks, it does not
# retract the old blob. Rewriting history is a force-push and is out of scope.
/agents/skill-lock.json

# Credentials and machine-local overrides
**/auth.json
**/hosts.yml
**/settings.local.json
**/*credential*
**/*token*
**/*secret*
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/known_hosts*
**/.netrc

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
private/

# Databases and caches
**/*.sqlite*
**/Cache/
**/CachedData/

# Histories and editor recovery data can contain private content
**/*history*
**/sessions/
**/logs/
**/swap/
**/undo/
**/view/
**/viminfo

# OS and archive noise
.DS_Store
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.*
*.dmg
